1
00:00:00,251 --> 00:00:01,252
Is this your plan?

2
00:00:01,335 --> 00:00:03,045
To be the next Mr. Aragon.

3
00:00:03,129 --> 00:00:04,755
I thought you were the head of PR.

4
00:00:04,839 --> 00:00:06,298
I wasn't aware
that you're an aspiring gigolo

5
00:00:06,382 --> 00:00:08,634
and a gold digger on the side.

6
00:00:08,718 --> 00:00:11,137
If I do want to go back to school,

7
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:13,973
I will be the one deciding.
Not because it's what she wants.

8
00:00:14,056 --> 00:00:17,351
And most especially not
because I owe her anything.

9
00:00:17,435 --> 00:00:18,853
-The partnership will pull through?
-Yes.

10
00:00:18,936 --> 00:00:21,272
We don't have problems anymore
because everything has been cleared

11
00:00:21,355 --> 00:00:25,109
and they value our competence
more than the rumors.

12
00:00:25,192 --> 00:00:27,778
So get to work.
Make sure everything is prepared.

13
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:33,617
I have nothing
to be ashamed of. I fought back.

14
00:00:33,701 --> 00:00:36,746
The victim should not
suffer embarrassment!

15
00:00:36,829 --> 00:00:39,707
Who should be embarrassed are the creator

16
00:00:39,790 --> 00:00:42,585
and the person
who showed it to the public.

17
00:00:42,668 --> 00:00:47,047
I will never let myself
be a mere victim in your eyes!

18
00:00:51,594 --> 00:00:53,095
I thought all the footage had been erased.

19
00:00:53,179 --> 00:00:55,222
Ricardo said he got rid of all the copies.

20
00:00:56,599 --> 00:00:58,058
He has all the copies?

21
00:00:58,934 --> 00:01:00,311
Then he leaked the video!

22
00:01:00,644 --> 00:01:02,229
Why would he do that?

23
00:01:02,730 --> 00:01:04,315
Why are you defending him?

24
00:01:04,648 --> 00:01:07,902
You know what happened to Patricia,
but you kept it from me!

25
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:11,697
Why didn't you tell Martin about this?

26
00:01:11,781 --> 00:01:13,407
What are you trying to prove?
That you're a hero?

27
00:01:13,491 --> 00:01:15,785
Martin is still Patricia's father.

28
00:01:15,868 --> 00:01:18,996
It was Patricia who decided
not to tell you.

29
00:01:19,371 --> 00:01:21,123
Whether she likes it or not,

30
00:01:21,499 --> 00:01:24,627
I have the right to know
because I'm her father!

31
00:01:24,710 --> 00:01:27,671
-I'm protecting my daughter!
-You let her get humiliated!

32
00:01:27,755 --> 00:01:30,049
Why is this my fault?

33
00:01:30,424 --> 00:01:32,551
You can't protect our daughter.

34
00:01:33,302 --> 00:01:36,889
I'm not surprised.
You've always been like that ever since.

35
00:01:41,185 --> 00:01:42,311
Martin.

36
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:56,302
That's the flash drive I brought in, sir.

37
00:02:56,385 --> 00:02:58,178
Then, where did that video come from?

38
00:02:58,262 --> 00:03:00,973
I swear, sir, I have nothing
to do with that video.

39
00:03:06,353 --> 00:03:08,188
I want to check the CCTV footage.

40
00:03:08,772 --> 00:03:10,566
We don't know how this happened, sir,

41
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:12,860
but the CCTV camera
in the control area isn't working.

42
00:03:13,652 --> 00:03:14,778
Let me see.

43
00:03:19,116 --> 00:03:20,284
-Clara.
-Yes, sir?

44
00:03:20,367 --> 00:03:21,952
Where are the people from Burger City?

45
00:03:22,286 --> 00:03:24,788
The transition team
went back to their area,

46
00:03:24,872 --> 00:03:27,249
but Mr. Smith went home already.

47
00:03:27,333 --> 00:03:29,752
Where's Ms. D, by the way?

48
00:03:29,835 --> 00:03:32,046
-I'll go check on her.
-Okay, sir. Excuse me.

49
00:03:32,504 --> 00:03:33,505
You!

50
00:03:38,427 --> 00:03:39,637
We're really sorry, Martin.

51
00:03:40,262 --> 00:03:42,097
We'll find out what happened.

52
00:03:42,181 --> 00:03:43,307
You bastard!

53
00:03:43,891 --> 00:03:45,684
You're the only one
who has a copy of that video!

54
00:03:48,145 --> 00:03:49,355
Are you accusing me?

55
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:50,981
Tell me.

56
00:03:51,482 --> 00:03:53,150
Where were you
when your daughter was in trouble?

57
00:03:53,609 --> 00:03:55,110
Shouldn't you be protecting her?

58
00:03:55,986 --> 00:03:57,321
You're useless!

59
00:03:58,072 --> 00:03:59,156
Hey!

60
00:03:59,615 --> 00:04:01,116
-Come on! Fight!
-Martin!

61
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,201
-Martin!
-Calm down.

62
00:04:02,284 --> 00:04:03,535
Let's fight!

63
00:04:04,286 --> 00:04:05,996
Is that all you can do?
Fight with your fists?

64
00:04:06,664 --> 00:04:07,831
-I'm sorry.
-That's enough.

65
00:04:08,540 --> 00:04:09,792
I don't fight weak people.

66
00:04:10,209 --> 00:04:12,628
-Martin!
-Martin, I said that's enough!

67
00:04:14,421 --> 00:04:16,674
Sir, there's a commotion
at the events room.

68
00:04:17,341 --> 00:04:18,467
What?

69
00:04:22,304 --> 00:04:23,806
Ricardo, Martin, stop it!

70
00:04:23,889 --> 00:04:25,057
-Sir!
-That's enough!

71
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:27,184
-Enough.
-Sir, please. Stop fighting.

72
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:28,644
-Stay out of this!
-Stop it!

73
00:04:31,730 --> 00:04:34,233
-Martin! Martin!
-Sir, that's enough.

74
00:04:34,316 --> 00:04:36,527
-Dad! Dad!
-Martin!

75
00:04:36,610 --> 00:04:37,945
-Dad!
-Patricia.

76
00:04:38,028 --> 00:04:39,113
-I'm sorry, Patricia.
-Come on.

77
00:04:39,446 --> 00:04:41,031
I didn't want to fight back,

78
00:04:41,573 --> 00:04:44,410
-but your father kept provoking me.
-You bastard!

79
00:04:44,493 --> 00:04:46,495
Patricia, please take your father outside.

80
00:04:46,578 --> 00:04:48,622
This is all your fault, Diana.

81
00:04:49,456 --> 00:04:52,334
Her life's been a mess since she got here!

82
00:04:53,002 --> 00:04:54,628
Don't you see?

83
00:04:54,712 --> 00:04:58,173
The people who want to destroy you
are also going after her!

84
00:04:58,257 --> 00:04:59,717
Dad, that's enough.

85
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:01,969
Let's go home. Come on.

86
00:05:05,848 --> 00:05:08,392
-That's enough.
-Let's go.

87
00:05:14,606 --> 00:05:15,649
Watch your step.

88
00:05:23,991 --> 00:05:25,409
Let me check your hand.

89
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,585
Dad, why did you do that?

90
00:05:34,668 --> 00:05:36,503
Why are you blaming your father?

91
00:05:37,838 --> 00:05:40,090
He was the one who got hurt.

92
00:05:44,887 --> 00:05:48,557
You're the one I should ask, Patricia.

93
00:05:49,475 --> 00:05:52,352
Why didn't you tell me
that happened to you?

94
00:05:54,521 --> 00:05:55,522
Why?

95
00:05:56,940 --> 00:06:00,360
I don't want to add to your problems.

96
00:06:00,444 --> 00:06:02,029
I don't want to be a burden.

97
00:06:02,362 --> 00:06:05,240
What, you think we can't protect you?

98
00:06:08,202 --> 00:06:09,870
You probably think…

99
00:06:10,954 --> 00:06:13,332
-I'm weak.
-No, Dad.

100
00:06:15,584 --> 00:06:17,002
Tell us, Patricia.

101
00:06:17,711 --> 00:06:19,505
Are we a burden to you?

102
00:06:21,131 --> 00:06:24,551
I mean, we'll be fine. I have a job now.

103
00:06:25,886 --> 00:06:27,930
I will not abandon you.

104
00:06:30,557 --> 00:06:32,935
You're not a burden to me.

105
00:06:35,395 --> 00:06:41,360
I'm doing all of this
because I love you all so much.

106
00:06:46,657 --> 00:06:47,783
Dear…

107
00:06:50,202 --> 00:06:52,663
I don't want you to lie to me.

108
00:06:52,746 --> 00:06:55,165
Don't keep secrets from me ever again.

109
00:06:57,709 --> 00:06:59,294
Promise me that.

110
00:07:00,587 --> 00:07:01,672
Yes, I promise.

111
00:07:01,755 --> 00:07:03,423
I'm sorry.

112
00:07:34,246 --> 00:07:36,081
You acted like kids.

113
00:07:41,086 --> 00:07:42,754
Who did this?

114
00:07:44,298 --> 00:07:45,757
We're still investigating.

115
00:07:45,841 --> 00:07:48,677
But whoever did it
has access to the control booth,

116
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:51,138
so that means they're part of La Familia.

117
00:07:53,056 --> 00:07:55,851
So, it's because of my enemy again?

118
00:07:59,646 --> 00:08:02,524
This is an attack against me.

119
00:08:03,650 --> 00:08:04,818
It's because of me.

120
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:08,697
They should've just attacked me instead.

121
00:08:10,991 --> 00:08:12,075
Why…

122
00:08:12,743 --> 00:08:15,370
Why would they drag my daughter into this?

123
00:08:16,413 --> 00:08:19,666
They should've just left
my daughter alone.

124
00:08:20,709 --> 00:08:23,795
Not my daughter. No.
They should direct their anger at me.

125
00:08:23,879 --> 00:08:26,924
It should be me, not her.
I'm the one they should attack.

126
00:08:30,969 --> 00:08:33,055
Not my daughter. No.

127
00:08:39,645 --> 00:08:41,396
-Sir, good evening.
-Hmm?

128
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:42,773
I'm Carlo Lozano.

129
00:08:43,565 --> 00:08:45,692
I'd like to file a report…

130
00:08:47,069 --> 00:08:48,320
about La Familia.

131
00:08:53,575 --> 00:08:55,160
Ms. D, Sir Ricardo…

132
00:08:55,911 --> 00:08:57,329
Have you found out what happened?

133
00:08:57,412 --> 00:08:59,665
The original AVP
on the control booth's computer

134
00:08:59,748 --> 00:09:01,124
was switched to Patricia's video.

135
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:03,001
There's also a technical problem
with the CCTV cameras,

136
00:09:03,085 --> 00:09:04,253
so there's no footage.

137
00:09:04,336 --> 00:09:06,255
That's… That's impossible.

138
00:09:06,338 --> 00:09:08,382
How did the security breach occur?

139
00:09:08,465 --> 00:09:10,467
Why don't we investigate
from where it all started?

140
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:12,469
You're the only one who has the video.

141
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:13,845
How come someone else got it?

142
00:09:14,304 --> 00:09:16,974
And why did they target
the sole heiress of La Familia?

143
00:09:17,391 --> 00:09:18,558
Teddy, what are you trying to imply?

144
00:09:18,642 --> 00:09:19,810
The truth!

145
00:09:22,688 --> 00:09:23,730
Mrs. Aragon.

146
00:09:23,814 --> 00:09:24,940
What now?

147
00:09:25,649 --> 00:09:26,650
Help!

148
00:09:29,861 --> 00:09:32,489
It's you! This is the guy who attacked me!

149
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:33,657
-How dare you!
-Ma'am!

150
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:35,826
-Damn you!
-Ma'am Diana, believe me.

151
00:09:35,909 --> 00:09:37,911
-I didn't want that to happen.
-Yes, right!

152
00:09:37,995 --> 00:09:39,204
I have no choice.

153
00:09:39,288 --> 00:09:40,372
I was paid to do it.

154
00:09:40,455 --> 00:09:41,915
But my conscience is eating me away.

155
00:09:41,999 --> 00:09:44,293
Who told you to do it?

156
00:09:45,127 --> 00:09:46,211
Tell me!

157
00:09:50,549 --> 00:09:51,633
It's him.

158
00:09:53,135 --> 00:09:54,261
Your brother.

159
00:09:55,053 --> 00:09:57,389
It was your brother who gave me orders.

160
00:09:57,806 --> 00:09:59,683
He ordered me to attack you.

161
00:10:00,809 --> 00:10:03,437
Liar! I don't know
what you're talking about!

162
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:04,896
I have proof.

163
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:07,899
Sir Teddy and I spoke
on the phone several times.

164
00:10:08,275 --> 00:10:10,402
He gives me instructions on what to do.

165
00:10:10,777 --> 00:10:12,779
He told me to decline
the settlement offer,

166
00:10:12,863 --> 00:10:14,531
prolong the negotiation process,

167
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:16,283
and stage a rally outside your office.

168
00:10:16,366 --> 00:10:18,285
-That's not true!
-But…

169
00:10:18,368 --> 00:10:21,788
when Ma'am Patricia talked
to some of our group members,

170
00:10:21,872 --> 00:10:24,750
they agreed to accept La Familia's offer.

171
00:10:25,292 --> 00:10:27,044
I couldn't convince them anymore,

172
00:10:27,669 --> 00:10:29,463
so he started to threaten me.

173
00:10:29,546 --> 00:10:33,300
He said I have to follow his orders
and attack Ma'am Diana.

174
00:10:33,383 --> 00:10:34,468
-Take that back!
-Teddy, relax.

175
00:10:34,551 --> 00:10:35,552
Don't touch me!

176
00:10:35,635 --> 00:10:37,554
-Relax.
-You were the one who gave him orders!

177
00:10:38,221 --> 00:10:41,350
-What are you talking about?
-You have his phone!

178
00:10:41,433 --> 00:10:42,601
You even threatened me!

179
00:10:43,268 --> 00:10:45,979
Diana, don't believe him. It's all a lie.

180
00:10:46,355 --> 00:10:47,689
He's out of his mind.

181
00:10:47,773 --> 00:10:49,107
Please, please, please.

182
00:10:49,191 --> 00:10:50,984
-Why?
-No, no.

183
00:10:51,068 --> 00:10:52,402
-No.
-Why?

184
00:10:53,403 --> 00:10:54,780
I'm your sister.

185
00:10:54,863 --> 00:10:56,281
-Yes.
-I'm your sister.

186
00:10:57,991 --> 00:10:59,951
We checked Carlo's phone,

187
00:11:00,327 --> 00:11:02,662
and we have confirmed his statement.

188
00:11:02,746 --> 00:11:04,748
-Give me that!
-Teddy!

189
00:11:04,831 --> 00:11:07,459
-Give me that! Give it to me!
-Sir! Sir! Wait!

190
00:11:07,542 --> 00:11:08,543
-Wait! Let go of me!
-Relax, sir.

191
00:11:08,627 --> 00:11:09,920
I said let go of me!

192
00:11:10,003 --> 00:11:11,338
-Let go of me!
-Come on!

193
00:11:11,421 --> 00:11:12,839
Ms. D.

194
00:11:12,923 --> 00:11:15,342
We found some footage
of what happened earlier.

195
00:11:15,425 --> 00:11:17,344
We didn't get anything from the CCTV,

196
00:11:17,427 --> 00:11:20,597
but the cameramen
were testing the cameras before the event.

197
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:23,683
They got a video of what was happening
at the control booth.

198
00:11:35,487 --> 00:11:36,780
It was Georgia who did it?

199
00:11:36,863 --> 00:11:38,740
That's not true! That's not true!

200
00:11:38,824 --> 00:11:40,117
It's fabricated! It's fake!

201
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:42,828
-It's fake!
-Shut up! Shut up, Teddy!

202
00:11:42,911 --> 00:11:43,995
Enough!

203
00:11:52,212 --> 00:11:53,880
Okay. Thanks, Enzo.

204
00:12:03,974 --> 00:12:05,267
What did he say?

205
00:12:06,393 --> 00:12:09,563
It was Uncle Teddy and Georgia
who released the video.

206
00:12:11,106 --> 00:12:12,774
Wait. How did they get the video?

207
00:12:12,858 --> 00:12:14,192
They don't know.

208
00:12:15,110 --> 00:12:16,945
The police are taking them
to the police station.

209
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:18,864
Those bastards!

210
00:12:18,947 --> 00:12:21,616
-Come on, let's go.
-No need, Dad.

211
00:12:22,117 --> 00:12:24,119
Let's leave it to them.
They can handle it.

212
00:12:25,078 --> 00:12:27,873
That family is really something.

213
00:12:28,290 --> 00:12:30,250
They spare no one.

214
00:12:30,959 --> 00:12:33,128
For what? For money?

215
00:12:33,837 --> 00:12:35,714
And they dragged you into all this?

216
00:12:37,466 --> 00:12:41,052
And what did your mother do?

217
00:12:41,595 --> 00:12:43,221
She didn't do anything, did she?

218
00:12:43,305 --> 00:12:45,891
You were the one who defended yourself.

219
00:12:45,974 --> 00:12:46,975
Mom, that's enough.

220
00:12:47,434 --> 00:12:50,187
Maybe you should quit your job
at La Familia.

221
00:12:50,812 --> 00:12:52,689
Hold on, Martin.

222
00:12:53,607 --> 00:12:56,276
Why would you want Patricia
to quit her job?

223
00:12:56,860 --> 00:13:00,530
She has to prove herself
to them more than ever.

224
00:13:01,907 --> 00:13:06,244
You're the only one
who has the right to inherit all that.

225
00:13:06,328 --> 00:13:09,456
They can all leave, but not you.

226
00:13:23,094 --> 00:13:24,596
-What are you doing?
-Hey!

227
00:13:25,931 --> 00:13:27,224
I can file charges for that.

228
00:13:29,684 --> 00:13:30,977
Diana asked me to come here.

229
00:13:31,061 --> 00:13:32,687
I don't need you!

230
00:13:33,813 --> 00:13:36,858
Bribery, obstruction of justice,

231
00:13:36,942 --> 00:13:39,945
serious physical injury, attempted murder.

232
00:13:41,321 --> 00:13:43,365
Those are some of the charges
that can be filed against you…

233
00:13:44,157 --> 00:13:46,409
based on Carlo's testimony and evidence.

234
00:13:47,619 --> 00:13:49,829
Do you think you can intimidate me?

235
00:13:51,039 --> 00:13:52,874
Just to remind you,

236
00:13:53,542 --> 00:13:54,584
I'm an Aragon.

237
00:13:55,961 --> 00:13:57,170
Teddy.

238
00:13:58,129 --> 00:14:01,800
Your being an Aragon is useless
if Diana decides to abandon you.

239
00:14:02,467 --> 00:14:06,096
Do you think you can
get away from all this, huh?

240
00:14:06,179 --> 00:14:07,556
Tell me.

241
00:14:07,931 --> 00:14:09,474
What's your problem, huh?

242
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:12,227
Why are you doing this?

243
00:14:12,310 --> 00:14:13,937
I'm not doing anything.

244
00:14:14,896 --> 00:14:16,773
I can see right through you.

245
00:14:20,777 --> 00:14:22,153
It takes one to know one?

246
00:14:23,321 --> 00:14:24,739
Our lawyers are on their way.

247
00:14:24,823 --> 00:14:26,700
You won't be able
to prove the accusations.

248
00:14:27,617 --> 00:14:30,787
You know, I could help you.

249
00:14:31,162 --> 00:14:32,831
We should be helping each other.

250
00:14:34,624 --> 00:14:36,585
But you did this to yourself.

251
00:14:39,754 --> 00:14:40,880
Hmm…

252
00:14:44,467 --> 00:14:46,636
Dad… Dad… Dad…

253
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:50,682
Dad, I don't want to go to jail.
I don't want to go to jail, Daddy!

254
00:14:55,937 --> 00:14:57,355
You see…

255
00:14:57,981 --> 00:15:00,775
ever since we were kids,

256
00:15:01,776 --> 00:15:03,695
Teddy felt like I was Dad's favorite.

257
00:15:06,823 --> 00:15:10,410
When he was younger,
he was always left alone.

258
00:15:12,037 --> 00:15:14,164
That's why he's constantly
seeking attention.

259
00:15:16,249 --> 00:15:17,876
He grew up…

260
00:15:19,085 --> 00:15:21,630
always needing to prove something.

261
00:15:23,048 --> 00:15:25,008
That he deserved more?

262
00:15:28,011 --> 00:15:31,222
Dad gave me all the responsibility.

263
00:15:35,727 --> 00:15:37,687
He told me I was the eldest.

264
00:15:38,188 --> 00:15:40,565
So I should act like one…

265
00:15:40,649 --> 00:15:43,026
and take care of my brother.

266
00:15:45,779 --> 00:15:47,697
I can't abandon him.

267
00:15:50,867 --> 00:15:52,619
I never meant…

268
00:15:53,453 --> 00:15:56,456
for us to compete.

269
00:15:58,249 --> 00:15:59,542
I think…

270
00:16:00,043 --> 00:16:01,878
he doesn't want to just compete with you.

271
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:04,881
He wants to beat you.

272
00:16:07,592 --> 00:16:10,887
So he doesn't care who gets hurt
as long as he wins.

273
00:16:12,931 --> 00:16:14,265
He even wants…

274
00:16:15,892 --> 00:16:17,102
to destroy Patricia.

275
00:16:21,147 --> 00:16:23,441
Maybe I'm just forcing…

276
00:16:24,901 --> 00:16:26,903
what I want on Patricia.

277
00:16:28,446 --> 00:16:31,574
But now she's getting dragged
into this mess.

278
00:16:33,868 --> 00:16:36,121
Maybe I really don't know…

279
00:16:38,123 --> 00:16:39,916
how to be a good mother.

280
00:16:42,794 --> 00:16:44,838
If only Patricia knew…

281
00:16:47,090 --> 00:16:49,175
I'm trying…

282
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:53,346
I'm trying to be a good mother.

283
00:16:54,264 --> 00:16:55,390
But…

284
00:16:57,642 --> 00:17:00,562
I wasn't raised to be soft.

285
00:17:04,858 --> 00:17:06,109
Sorry.

286
00:17:06,609 --> 00:17:07,694
It's okay.

287
00:17:09,988 --> 00:17:12,157
Why did you bring me here anyway?

288
00:17:14,117 --> 00:17:17,412
We are here to… let it all out.

289
00:17:19,497 --> 00:17:22,959
If you're angry… if you want to curse…

290
00:17:23,752 --> 00:17:24,836
if you want to scream,

291
00:17:24,919 --> 00:17:26,045
let it out.

292
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:29,048
-No.
-Curse them all out. Like this.

293
00:17:30,258 --> 00:17:31,509
You animals!

294
00:17:32,802 --> 00:17:34,554
You bastards!

295
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:37,640
-Uh…
-Try it.

296
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:40,351
I don't think so.

297
00:17:40,435 --> 00:17:42,937
Come on, Diana. You can do it. Try it.

298
00:17:49,444 --> 00:17:50,820
You shameless bastards!

299
00:17:53,406 --> 00:17:54,908
Diana, you can do better than that.

300
00:17:54,991 --> 00:17:56,868
Come on. Scream.

301
00:17:56,951 --> 00:17:58,161
Let it out!

302
00:17:58,703 --> 00:18:00,205
Curse them out.

303
00:18:06,044 --> 00:18:07,921
You shameless bastards!

304
00:18:08,588 --> 00:18:10,381
You animals!

305
00:18:11,174 --> 00:18:13,259
You demons!

306
00:18:14,552 --> 00:18:16,805
Damn all of you!

307
00:18:27,732 --> 00:18:30,944
I'm not a bad person.

308
00:18:31,986 --> 00:18:34,489
I'm a good person.

309
00:18:34,572 --> 00:18:38,660
I did everything for my family.

310
00:18:39,786 --> 00:18:43,748
I did everything for them.

311
00:18:43,832 --> 00:18:44,833
It's okay.

312
00:18:45,792 --> 00:18:48,711
This is just how I was raised.

313
00:18:48,795 --> 00:18:51,881
This is how my father raised me.

314
00:18:53,007 --> 00:18:54,843
I'm not a bad person.

315
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:57,136
It's okay. It's okay.

316
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:08,189
Thank you, Attorney.

317
00:19:08,773 --> 00:19:10,567
But this isn't over yet, Teddy.

318
00:19:10,650 --> 00:19:12,861
They'll still investigate you thoroughly.

319
00:19:12,944 --> 00:19:14,153
I'm ready.

320
00:19:15,405 --> 00:19:17,991
Just make sure
my daughter doesn't get charged.

321
00:19:18,074 --> 00:19:20,535
Georgia's case will be easy to resolve.

322
00:19:20,618 --> 00:19:22,495
They won't find any evidence against her.

323
00:19:22,579 --> 00:19:24,497
You have nothing to worry about.

324
00:19:24,581 --> 00:19:25,707
Okay?

325
00:19:26,749 --> 00:19:29,043
-We'll be in touch.
-Okay.

326
00:19:42,473 --> 00:19:43,600
Sir.

327
00:19:44,684 --> 00:19:46,519
Ms. D wants to speak with you.

328
00:19:50,481 --> 00:19:51,691
Sis.

329
00:19:52,025 --> 00:19:53,359
It wasn't me.

330
00:19:53,902 --> 00:19:55,320
I didn't do it.

331
00:19:57,655 --> 00:19:59,115
Why did you do that?

332
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:01,117
How could you do that to me?

333
00:20:02,911 --> 00:20:06,456
Everything Carlo said was a lie.

334
00:20:07,624 --> 00:20:09,000
They're not true. He's lying.

335
00:20:09,083 --> 00:20:11,210
-Oh, come on.
-I could never hurt you.

336
00:20:11,711 --> 00:20:14,505
I could never hurt you.
Why would I even do that?

337
00:20:14,881 --> 00:20:17,592
And someone gave me that USB.

338
00:20:17,967 --> 00:20:20,178
They said it was urgent
and needed for the program.

339
00:20:20,261 --> 00:20:22,096
So, I just gave it to them.

340
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:24,015
Please, Sis…

341
00:20:24,557 --> 00:20:26,976
Please believe me.

342
00:20:27,060 --> 00:20:29,145
I admit I wasn't careful.

343
00:20:29,228 --> 00:20:31,606
I let someone who wanted
to hurt you use me.

344
00:20:31,689 --> 00:20:33,858
-It's my fault, but I--
-Oh, come on!

345
00:20:33,942 --> 00:20:37,070
Come on, Teddy! Don't take me for a fool!

346
00:20:38,071 --> 00:20:39,781
You're so shameless!

347
00:20:40,323 --> 00:20:43,409
-You're an ingrate!
-Sis, please…

348
00:20:43,493 --> 00:20:46,829
-How could you do that, Teddy?
-Sis, please believe me…

349
00:20:47,330 --> 00:20:49,958
Please believe me!

350
00:20:50,041 --> 00:20:51,334
-Get up!
-Please, Sis!

351
00:20:51,417 --> 00:20:53,795
-I said get--
-I'm begging you! Please…

352
00:20:54,212 --> 00:20:56,464
-Teddy, get up!
-Please believe me!

353
00:20:56,547 --> 00:20:58,299
I could never do that to you!

354
00:20:58,633 --> 00:21:00,969
Sis, I could never do that to you…

355
00:21:01,719 --> 00:21:05,348
Please. I didn't do it!

356
00:21:05,932 --> 00:21:07,809
Please believe me…

357
00:21:11,354 --> 00:21:12,730
Diana…

358
00:21:13,231 --> 00:21:16,150
-Sis… Sis…
-How could you…

359
00:21:16,234 --> 00:21:19,237
How could you do that to me?

360
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:20,905
-My goodness, Teddy!
-Sis…

361
00:21:22,281 --> 00:21:23,366
Please…

362
00:21:23,449 --> 00:21:25,660
I'm your big sister.

363
00:21:26,786 --> 00:21:28,371
Come on.

364
00:21:28,913 --> 00:21:33,459
Do you remember that I was the one
who took care of you when you were little?

365
00:21:34,168 --> 00:21:38,756
I was the one Dad would scold
whenever you did something wrong!

366
00:21:39,465 --> 00:21:41,926
Dad always reminded me

367
00:21:42,385 --> 00:21:46,681
I should be responsible
because I'm your big sister.

368
00:21:46,764 --> 00:21:51,394
I'm sorry. Sis… Sis… Sis, please…

369
00:21:52,603 --> 00:21:56,065
Whenever you'd cause trouble,

370
00:21:56,149 --> 00:22:00,486
I was blamed and punished, too!

371
00:22:01,112 --> 00:22:02,905
You bastard!

372
00:22:02,989 --> 00:22:04,699
Sis… Sis…

373
00:22:04,782 --> 00:22:07,535
Dad always told me…

374
00:22:07,618 --> 00:22:09,620
we're a family. And family…

375
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:14,500
should always look out
for each other no matter what!

376
00:22:15,752 --> 00:22:18,296
But to what limit?

377
00:22:19,213 --> 00:22:22,675
You also hurt my family, Teddy!

378
00:22:23,009 --> 00:22:27,513
Patricia's my daughter, remember?
She's also your family, you bastard!

379
00:22:27,597 --> 00:22:29,724
I'm sorry, Sis.

380
00:22:29,807 --> 00:22:30,975
You bastard.

381
00:22:31,309 --> 00:22:33,561
How dare you!

382
00:22:33,644 --> 00:22:37,482
-You're so shameless!
-Sis…

383
00:22:37,857 --> 00:22:38,858
Sis…

384
00:22:40,026 --> 00:22:41,861
Sis…

385
00:23:17,563 --> 00:23:18,731
Patricia.

386
00:23:20,983 --> 00:23:22,110
Wow.

387
00:23:23,277 --> 00:23:24,320
Chin up.

388
00:23:27,532 --> 00:23:29,700
Don't worry about me, sir.
I can handle it.

389
00:23:31,577 --> 00:23:32,787
It's okay if you can't.

390
00:23:35,623 --> 00:23:36,749
Thank you.

391
00:23:38,459 --> 00:23:39,752
You've got this.

392
00:23:47,426 --> 00:23:50,805
-Oh, there's Patricia.
-Let's go.

393
00:23:50,888 --> 00:23:53,015
-Patricia.
-Patricia, are you okay?

394
00:23:53,099 --> 00:23:55,893
Don't think about it anymore.

395
00:23:56,811 --> 00:23:58,479
We believe you, friend.

396
00:23:58,813 --> 00:24:02,150
I hope they catch whoever did that to you.

397
00:24:02,733 --> 00:24:06,195
You're a good person.
They shouldn't have done that to you.

398
00:24:06,279 --> 00:24:07,738
-Mm-hmm.
-Keep fighting.

399
00:24:07,822 --> 00:24:09,365
You got this, girl!

400
00:24:09,448 --> 00:24:10,992
-You've got this.
-Thank you.

401
00:24:11,075 --> 00:24:12,660
-Thank you, everyone.
-We're here for you.

402
00:24:12,743 --> 00:24:14,120
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

403
00:24:28,467 --> 00:24:29,802
Are you okay?

404
00:24:39,437 --> 00:24:41,689
You should be recycled.

405
00:24:43,649 --> 00:24:44,901
Plastic.

406
00:24:45,610 --> 00:24:48,237
Enzo told me what happened last night.

407
00:24:52,366 --> 00:24:55,328
Did he also tell you
there's no evidence against me?

408
00:24:57,413 --> 00:24:58,748
That's why I'm here.

409
00:24:59,832 --> 00:25:01,500
You're so shameless.

410
00:25:01,584 --> 00:25:04,545
It was an honest mistake!

411
00:25:04,629 --> 00:25:07,340
How was I supposed to know
that USB had your filthy video?

412
00:25:08,841 --> 00:25:11,219
But you know what? You are the mistake.

413
00:25:11,928 --> 00:25:14,347
I hope Aunt Diana never let you in here.

414
00:25:14,931 --> 00:25:17,558
Because no matter how much
you pretend to be talented,

415
00:25:17,975 --> 00:25:21,229
you will never amount to anything.

416
00:25:22,688 --> 00:25:24,899
You have nothing to show for yourself.

417
00:25:27,485 --> 00:25:28,569
Patricia, what are you doing?

418
00:25:28,653 --> 00:25:29,779
-Let go--
-Between the two of us,

419
00:25:29,862 --> 00:25:31,864
you're the useless one.

420
00:25:31,948 --> 00:25:34,325
If you were so talented,
you wouldn't have to humiliate me

421
00:25:34,408 --> 00:25:36,744
-just to secure your position here!
-Let go of me, Patricia!

422
00:25:36,827 --> 00:25:38,204
Come on!

423
00:25:39,956 --> 00:25:42,333
Don't push me, Georgia.

424
00:25:42,792 --> 00:25:44,252
I fight back.

425
00:25:44,835 --> 00:25:46,420
Don't test my patience.

426
00:25:47,255 --> 00:25:48,631
Remember…

427
00:25:49,173 --> 00:25:50,549
Between the two of us,

428
00:25:50,633 --> 00:25:53,970
I am more worthy.

429
00:25:54,637 --> 00:25:56,138
-Okay?
-Let go of me.

430
00:26:10,069 --> 00:26:11,153
Argh!

431
00:26:14,615 --> 00:26:17,326
What are you doing?
Where are you taking this?

432
00:26:17,410 --> 00:26:18,411
Give it to me! Give it!

433
00:26:19,245 --> 00:26:20,454
What's this?

434
00:26:23,541 --> 00:26:26,377
Sir Teddy, you're being transferred.

435
00:26:27,169 --> 00:26:28,212
Ms. D's orders.

436
00:26:28,546 --> 00:26:29,755
What? She's demoting me?

437
00:26:30,172 --> 00:26:32,425
-Lateral transfer.
-What position?

438
00:26:33,467 --> 00:26:35,553
I can't be removed as CMO.

439
00:26:35,636 --> 00:26:38,180
You're being transferred
to Marketing and Distribution

440
00:26:38,264 --> 00:26:40,099
as Executive Director.

441
00:26:40,182 --> 00:26:41,767
If you have any questions,

442
00:26:41,851 --> 00:26:44,061
you have a scheduled meeting with HR.

443
00:26:44,145 --> 00:26:46,480
They will introduce your new team,
discuss your scopes,

444
00:26:46,564 --> 00:26:48,649
-and--
-You can't do this!

445
00:26:49,608 --> 00:26:50,860
You can't do this, okay?

446
00:26:50,943 --> 00:26:54,488
I'll talk to her myself.
I've even apologized to her.

447
00:26:55,656 --> 00:26:57,325
Why did you apologize to her?

448
00:26:59,910 --> 00:27:03,039
I'm the one you and your daughter hurt.

449
00:27:09,420 --> 00:27:13,257
You didn't expect that I'd fight back.

450
00:27:14,675 --> 00:27:16,677
I'm no pushover.

451
00:27:19,055 --> 00:27:20,389
Patricia, look…

452
00:27:22,850 --> 00:27:24,060
I'm sorry.

453
00:27:26,562 --> 00:27:27,897
Okay? I'm sorry.

454
00:27:30,066 --> 00:27:31,192
Patricia.

455
00:27:31,692 --> 00:27:33,486
Ms. D needs to speak with you.

456
00:27:49,085 --> 00:27:52,463
My arm still hurts because of that woman.

457
00:27:52,922 --> 00:27:54,507
That bitch Patricia.

458
00:27:55,091 --> 00:27:56,759
You should've seen her earlier.

459
00:27:56,842 --> 00:28:00,096
Oh, she's really violent.

460
00:28:00,179 --> 00:28:01,722
Are you okay?

461
00:28:01,806 --> 00:28:03,432
Obviously not.

462
00:28:03,516 --> 00:28:06,018
What did you say?
What did Patricia do to you?

463
00:28:06,102 --> 00:28:07,395
I'll go now.

464
00:28:08,896 --> 00:28:10,106
Nothing.

465
00:28:10,648 --> 00:28:12,274
Nothing?

466
00:28:12,733 --> 00:28:15,903
I heard you. So, what did Patricia do?

467
00:28:16,987 --> 00:28:19,615
Patricia blames me for the video,

468
00:28:20,241 --> 00:28:23,160
but I really had nothing
to do with it. Okay?

469
00:28:23,244 --> 00:28:26,747
I just don't like how he treats my dad
in this company.

470
00:28:27,415 --> 00:28:29,333
Hey. Ouch! Excuse me?

471
00:28:36,257 --> 00:28:39,552
You just need some ointment.

472
00:28:39,635 --> 00:28:40,761
Here.

473
00:28:41,178 --> 00:28:43,222
If you ever need anything,

474
00:28:43,305 --> 00:28:45,015
don't hesitate to come to me.

475
00:28:47,685 --> 00:28:49,854
But aren't you Patricia's mom?

476
00:28:52,189 --> 00:28:54,024
Stepmom.

477
00:28:54,108 --> 00:28:56,610
Diana is her mother. Take this.

478
00:28:57,278 --> 00:28:58,696
Just give that back to me later.

479
00:29:17,173 --> 00:29:19,133
Evil stepmom…

480
00:29:36,066 --> 00:29:37,318
You called for me?

481
00:29:40,154 --> 00:29:41,155
How are you?

482
00:29:42,072 --> 00:29:45,242
I don't really have a choice
but to be okay.

483
00:29:58,214 --> 00:29:59,423
What's this?

484
00:30:02,760 --> 00:30:04,220
Your full payment.

485
00:30:04,929 --> 00:30:07,181
That's the remaining balance
of 800,000 pesos.

486
00:30:11,810 --> 00:30:12,853
Why?

487
00:30:15,481 --> 00:30:17,358
You want to silence me
about what happened?

488
00:30:18,150 --> 00:30:19,777
To cover up for Uncle Teddy?

489
00:30:22,321 --> 00:30:23,531
Is that what you think?

490
00:30:24,615 --> 00:30:25,783
Isn't it?

491
00:30:26,992 --> 00:30:30,120
I thought that's what you wanted.
Full payment.

492
00:30:31,038 --> 00:30:32,831
You're just giving it to me
just like that?

493
00:30:35,376 --> 00:30:39,838
Patricia, I am giving you a chance
to take control of your own life.

494
00:30:40,673 --> 00:30:43,968
So you can decide what to do next.

495
00:30:44,051 --> 00:30:48,305
Because I don't ever want you
to think I'm holding you back.

496
00:30:49,223 --> 00:30:50,849
You're playing the good guy again.

497
00:30:55,396 --> 00:30:57,481
It's so easy for you
to give up on me, isn't it?

498
00:31:00,693 --> 00:31:01,902
Well…

499
00:31:04,446 --> 00:31:06,156
you never defended me, anyway.

500
00:31:13,539 --> 00:31:16,125
A lot of people are waiting
for my downfall.

501
00:31:16,500 --> 00:31:18,294
And they'd drag you down with me.

502
00:31:21,380 --> 00:31:23,048
I'm protecting you.

503
00:31:58,709 --> 00:31:59,877
Are you leaving?

504
00:32:09,261 --> 00:32:10,471
What do you think?

505
00:32:12,222 --> 00:32:14,141
Should I make my life easy?

506
00:32:15,351 --> 00:32:16,602
Should I leave all of this?

507
00:32:20,230 --> 00:32:21,398
That would be a waste.

508
00:32:23,817 --> 00:32:25,361
You're good, Patricia.

509
00:32:27,571 --> 00:32:29,323
And you matter here.

510
00:32:32,076 --> 00:32:33,202
I mean…

511
00:32:34,286 --> 00:32:36,288
You are an asset to this company.

512
00:32:37,581 --> 00:32:41,126
And no matter what happened,
I know you can bounce back.

513
00:32:41,460 --> 00:32:45,422
Plus, you're growing close
to the people here.

514
00:32:46,382 --> 00:32:48,425
A lot of people believe in you, Patricia.

515
00:32:51,553 --> 00:32:54,264
For the first time,
you and Ms. D see differently, huh?

516
00:33:00,270 --> 00:33:02,398
Who told you that
we see things differently?

517
00:33:09,780 --> 00:33:11,323
What does that check mean?

518
00:33:12,157 --> 00:33:13,992
I've seen this before in TV shows.

519
00:33:15,119 --> 00:33:18,539
She just wants you
to make decisions for yourself.

520
00:33:19,915 --> 00:33:21,333
Well, isn't that what you want?

521
00:33:22,292 --> 00:33:26,880
She wants to protect her eldest child.

522
00:33:27,881 --> 00:33:31,343
Huh? Eldest?
You don't have siblings, right?

523
00:33:33,721 --> 00:33:35,139
La Familia!

524
00:33:36,724 --> 00:33:41,103
La Familia comes first.

525
00:33:42,104 --> 00:33:45,232
Only La Familia matters.

526
00:33:46,275 --> 00:33:47,276
Because of me,

527
00:33:47,818 --> 00:33:52,865
the great reputation
of La Familia is ruined.

528
00:33:54,950 --> 00:33:56,535
That's why she wants me gone.

529
00:34:02,124 --> 00:34:04,585
I am the dead weight.

530
00:34:05,544 --> 00:34:07,045
I am the disgrace.

531
00:34:08,005 --> 00:34:10,591
I am worthless.

532
00:34:11,842 --> 00:34:13,802
That's not true, Patricia.

533
00:34:14,219 --> 00:34:15,637
That's not true.

534
00:34:16,430 --> 00:34:17,431
If you leave,

535
00:34:18,098 --> 00:34:21,351
it's like telling those who dislike you
that you've lost.

536
00:34:21,727 --> 00:34:23,687
That your name really has been ruined.

537
00:34:24,062 --> 00:34:27,149
Don't give them the satisfaction
of thinking you gave up.

538
00:34:28,108 --> 00:34:29,276
Instead,

539
00:34:29,359 --> 00:34:32,654
prove to them
why you deserve to be here at La Familia.

540
00:34:44,291 --> 00:34:45,501
Are you okay, Patricia?

541
00:34:45,584 --> 00:34:47,002
Mm, I'm clocking out.

542
00:34:50,672 --> 00:34:51,882
Patricia.

543
00:34:53,967 --> 00:34:55,010
Sir.

544
00:34:56,303 --> 00:34:58,388
-Going home?
-Yes, sir.

545
00:34:59,932 --> 00:35:01,683
I heard you talked to Diana.

546
00:35:04,853 --> 00:35:07,231
News travels fast here in La Familia, huh.

547
00:35:09,441 --> 00:35:13,278
-Have you made a decision?
-I'll think about it first.

548
00:35:13,779 --> 00:35:16,907
If you ask me, don't leave just yet.

549
00:35:17,282 --> 00:35:20,035
But if you think it's time
for you to leave,

550
00:35:21,203 --> 00:35:22,871
no one should stop you.

551
00:35:25,457 --> 00:35:26,959
Follow your dreams.

552
00:35:28,252 --> 00:35:30,712
In the short time we've had here,

553
00:35:30,796 --> 00:35:35,759
you've only ever succeeded
by following your heart.

554
00:35:40,973 --> 00:35:43,225
-All right, I'll go ahead.
-Take care.

555
00:35:50,607 --> 00:35:52,317
It's no joke how many times
you made us come back

556
00:35:52,401 --> 00:35:54,862
-just to get our money.
-Give me a break.

557
00:35:54,945 --> 00:35:56,864
What matters is that you're getting paid.

558
00:35:56,947 --> 00:36:00,158
-What if we asked for interest?
-There's no need for that.

559
00:36:12,421 --> 00:36:14,423
Please count it. That's complete.

560
00:36:14,798 --> 00:36:17,801
-We're all paid up.
-Go on now, you can leave.

561
00:36:18,343 --> 00:36:20,012
-Thank you very much.
-Thank you. Thank you.

562
00:36:20,095 --> 00:36:22,097
-Thank you.
-Thank you, Patricia.

563
00:36:28,729 --> 00:36:30,689
Dear, where did you get the money?

564
00:36:31,273 --> 00:36:33,275
Ms. D gave the full payment.

565
00:36:38,447 --> 00:36:41,325
Does that mean
you can leave La Familia now?

566
00:36:43,076 --> 00:36:47,497
What if Patricia leaves for good?

567
00:36:54,004 --> 00:36:55,297
Back to how it was.

568
00:36:56,006 --> 00:37:00,594
Whatever I do,
she still thinks badly of me.

569
00:37:02,095 --> 00:37:04,723
-Has anything changed?
-Yes.

570
00:37:07,434 --> 00:37:10,979
Even if you don't tell me, I can feel it.

571
00:37:12,689 --> 00:37:16,610
Before, you only protected La Familia.

572
00:37:17,694 --> 00:37:19,863
Now, you protect Patricia too.

573
00:37:21,239 --> 00:37:23,283
You're blaming yourself.

574
00:37:24,451 --> 00:37:27,329
You've never given up on La Familia.

575
00:37:28,455 --> 00:37:32,960
I wish you were like that
with Patricia too.

576
00:37:37,005 --> 00:37:39,049
I didn't give up on Patricia.

577
00:37:42,552 --> 00:37:48,433
How can I protect her
if she doesn't trust me?

578
00:37:50,227 --> 00:37:53,146
Sometimes the heart acts before the mind.

579
00:37:57,359 --> 00:37:58,485
Diana…

580
00:38:00,570 --> 00:38:03,907
don't let your relationship
be ruined, okay?

581
00:38:05,867 --> 00:38:08,370
You should fight together.

582
00:38:48,201 --> 00:38:51,955
So, have you made your decision?

583
00:38:53,206 --> 00:38:55,542
I've paid off my father's debt in full.

584
00:38:56,543 --> 00:38:57,669
Good.

585
00:38:58,754 --> 00:39:00,422
Your father won't be
a problem for you anymore.

586
00:39:02,007 --> 00:39:05,427
You can do what you want for yourself now.

587
00:39:09,306 --> 00:39:10,515
You're right.

588
00:39:12,350 --> 00:39:13,727
So, I've made my decision.

589
00:39:16,313 --> 00:39:17,856
I'm not leaving.

590
00:39:27,866 --> 00:39:29,534
-Will that get filled?
-Yes.

591
00:39:29,618 --> 00:39:30,952
-Expecting a big win?
-You know how it is…

592
00:39:31,036 --> 00:39:32,662
-Remember our deal, okay?
-Hey, guys.

593
00:39:32,746 --> 00:39:33,747
-Hey, man!
-Martin!

594
00:39:33,830 --> 00:39:36,374
-You're starting early today.
-Want to place a bet?

595
00:39:36,458 --> 00:39:37,626
What's that?

596
00:39:38,043 --> 00:39:39,127
Ending.

597
00:39:41,505 --> 00:39:42,589
Sure. Hold on.

598
00:39:42,672 --> 00:39:45,133
-That's what I'm talking about!
-Here's 200 pesos.

599
00:39:45,217 --> 00:39:47,010
0-9 and 0-1.

600
00:39:47,094 --> 00:39:48,970
-All right then.
-Nice.

601
00:39:49,054 --> 00:39:50,305
Come join us for a bit.

602
00:39:50,388 --> 00:39:52,015
-Come here.
-Yes, sit right here with us.

603
00:39:52,099 --> 00:39:54,059
Sure. Hold on a second.

604
00:39:54,434 --> 00:39:55,519
Here.

605
00:39:56,269 --> 00:39:57,312
-I'll just log this in.
-Go ahead.

606
00:39:59,064 --> 00:40:00,607
Have a shot first.

607
00:40:01,191 --> 00:40:03,902
Well, it's still early.

608
00:40:08,865 --> 00:40:09,908
-That's it.
-There you go.

609
00:40:09,991 --> 00:40:11,910
Why? Do you have somewhere to be?

610
00:40:13,120 --> 00:40:15,372
Why? Do you guys have jobs?

611
00:40:15,747 --> 00:40:16,998
There aren't any gigs.

612
00:40:17,791 --> 00:40:20,001
My wife has a job,
she earns her own money.

613
00:40:22,129 --> 00:40:23,839
My kid just got paid.

614
00:40:23,922 --> 00:40:26,758
Well… you guys are still strong.

615
00:40:27,467 --> 00:40:29,261
You drink pretty hard.

616
00:40:29,761 --> 00:40:31,972
I raised and supported my kids.

617
00:40:32,055 --> 00:40:34,474
Naturally, it's their turn to support me.

618
00:40:34,558 --> 00:40:37,185
We should really benefit
from our children.

619
00:40:38,103 --> 00:40:39,229
It doesn't work that way.

620
00:40:40,272 --> 00:40:42,023
Come on, we're the same, Martin!

621
00:40:42,107 --> 00:40:46,570
The only difference is your daughter
will be a millionaire.

622
00:40:46,903 --> 00:40:48,405
You're just waiting to hit it big, right?

623
00:40:49,573 --> 00:40:50,699
-Drink up for the jackpot.
-Yes, jackpot.

624
00:40:50,782 --> 00:40:53,034
Guys, I'm not relying on my daughter.

625
00:40:54,327 --> 00:40:56,496
I'm just looking for an opportunity
to bounce back.

626
00:40:57,122 --> 00:40:58,623
I'm going to start my own business.

627
00:40:59,583 --> 00:41:01,334
Sure, whatever you say.

628
00:41:01,418 --> 00:41:03,545
-Come on, let's drink.
-Let's drink to that!

629
00:41:03,628 --> 00:41:04,963
-Drink up.
-Hold on.

630
00:41:05,046 --> 00:41:06,756
-My kids are here.
-Wait, finish this first.

631
00:41:06,840 --> 00:41:08,967
-Hey, just this one!
-Next time, next time.

632
00:41:09,050 --> 00:41:10,468
-Thanks, appreciate it.
-I know, right?

633
00:41:10,552 --> 00:41:12,429
-Drink all of it.
-Bless me, Dad.

634
00:41:12,512 --> 00:41:13,680
-Go on inside.
-That's fine.

635
00:41:13,763 --> 00:41:15,015
-Mm-hmm.
-Here you go.

636
00:41:15,098 --> 00:41:17,225
-Are you tired? You okay?
-Another shot.

637
00:41:17,309 --> 00:41:18,643
It's tiring, Dad.

638
00:41:18,727 --> 00:41:20,562
If nobody wins here…

639
00:41:20,645 --> 00:41:22,147
-It's ours.
-Of course!

640
00:41:22,230 --> 00:41:25,567
-We'll take it all.
-Shot, shot!

641
00:41:25,650 --> 00:41:29,905
As per your instructions,
I talked to the lawyers about Teddy.

642
00:41:31,031 --> 00:41:34,492
I also told the witnesses
not to release these yet.

643
00:41:34,576 --> 00:41:38,079
I'm having them gather their statements,
so at least we have something.

644
00:41:38,997 --> 00:41:41,124
But essentially,
it's a closed case for now.

645
00:41:43,376 --> 00:41:44,502
Okay.

646
00:41:50,425 --> 00:41:51,468
Yes?

647
00:41:53,261 --> 00:41:54,638
Diana, are you sure?

648
00:41:55,096 --> 00:41:57,140
What do you expect me to do, Ricardo?

649
00:41:58,683 --> 00:42:00,518
Power grab? Scheming?

650
00:42:01,228 --> 00:42:03,813
It won't help the company
if that comes out.

651
00:42:03,897 --> 00:42:05,190
Teddy is my brother.

652
00:42:07,025 --> 00:42:10,320
But they'll still think
you're favoring him.

653
00:42:11,488 --> 00:42:13,406
I manage what I can control.

654
00:42:13,823 --> 00:42:15,200
Teddy is one of them.

655
00:42:16,993 --> 00:42:21,248
Now, if our suspicions about him are true,

656
00:42:22,332 --> 00:42:24,376
he can't bring me down anyway.

657
00:42:25,502 --> 00:42:27,170
He's not that competent,

658
00:42:27,754 --> 00:42:30,799
and his influence in the company
isn't that broad.

659
00:42:31,925 --> 00:42:34,678
And what makes you think
I won't hold him accountable?

660
00:42:35,220 --> 00:42:37,472
I'll make sure he learns his lesson.

661
00:42:39,891 --> 00:42:43,353
You're not deciding
as the CEO of La Familia.

662
00:42:44,771 --> 00:42:46,856
You're deciding as a sister.

663
00:42:49,317 --> 00:42:51,152
That's what Dad taught us.

664
00:42:51,611 --> 00:42:54,698
Never to wash our dirty linen in public.

665
00:42:55,532 --> 00:42:59,411
Because those who want to bring us down

666
00:42:59,494 --> 00:43:01,788
will use that as ammo against us.

667
00:43:03,290 --> 00:43:05,834
Why? Do you have
a lot of dirty laundry hidden?

668
00:43:07,836 --> 00:43:09,004
We're done here.

669
00:43:11,339 --> 00:43:12,465
Okay.

670
00:43:22,225 --> 00:43:23,268
Are you all right?

671
00:43:24,185 --> 00:43:25,312
Sir.

672
00:43:27,105 --> 00:43:28,189
I'm fine.

673
00:43:28,273 --> 00:43:30,650
Looks like you want
to kick someone in real life.

674
00:43:31,901 --> 00:43:33,028
Who? Teddy?

675
00:43:37,240 --> 00:43:41,119
Well, Diana doesn't want the news to leak.

676
00:43:41,953 --> 00:43:43,621
That's why she won't press charges.

677
00:43:45,707 --> 00:43:46,833
Yes, I get that.

678
00:43:47,667 --> 00:43:50,003
When did she not put La Familia first?

679
00:43:51,254 --> 00:43:55,258
Nothing matters more
than the company's reputation.

680
00:43:56,384 --> 00:43:58,428
What is my humiliation worth to her?

681
00:43:59,971 --> 00:44:02,640
Patricia, Diana is just doing
what she thinks is right.

682
00:44:03,099 --> 00:44:04,559
For herself.

683
00:44:04,642 --> 00:44:05,727
For your family.

684
00:44:06,227 --> 00:44:09,105
Maybe she thinks when she retires,

685
00:44:10,148 --> 00:44:12,192
she'll have no one else
to rely on but Teddy.

686
00:44:13,109 --> 00:44:15,111
Teddy will continue La Familia.

687
00:44:16,905 --> 00:44:19,074
You have no interest in La Familia, right?

688
00:44:20,992 --> 00:44:22,494
I was surprised you lasted.

689
00:44:22,744 --> 00:44:24,496
I didn't stay for her.

690
00:44:25,914 --> 00:44:27,332
I'm here

691
00:44:28,416 --> 00:44:32,587
to prove to all of them that I can do it.

692
00:44:34,089 --> 00:44:36,091
It's hard to prove yourself…

693
00:44:38,551 --> 00:44:40,053
to someone who doesn't trust you.

694
00:44:40,136 --> 00:44:41,888
But I trust you.

695
00:44:43,264 --> 00:44:44,641
I know you can do it.

696
00:44:46,851 --> 00:44:48,269
So don't worry,

697
00:44:48,895 --> 00:44:52,607
just because Teddy got away
with what he did to you…

698
00:44:54,067 --> 00:44:55,527
doesn't mean he won't pay.

699
00:44:59,823 --> 00:45:01,324
What do you mean?

700
00:45:02,075 --> 00:45:04,744
Patricia, people like Teddy…

701
00:45:05,537 --> 00:45:07,163
won't stop

702
00:45:08,123 --> 00:45:10,083
until they get what they want.

703
00:45:11,543 --> 00:45:13,253
They won't stop pulling foolish tricks.

704
00:45:13,628 --> 00:45:15,130
But don't worry.

705
00:45:15,755 --> 00:45:18,258
If he does something stupid,
I'll be there to stop him.

706
00:45:18,341 --> 00:45:19,926
And I'll make sure

707
00:45:20,844 --> 00:45:23,221
even his name won't be able
to save him anymore.

708
00:45:28,435 --> 00:45:30,186
Why are you doing this?

709
00:45:33,189 --> 00:45:34,732
Because we're on the same side.

710
00:45:37,652 --> 00:45:39,529
I can see myself in you.

711
00:45:40,989 --> 00:45:42,740
I started from the bottom as well.

712
00:45:42,824 --> 00:45:44,742
I worked my way up without anyone's help.

713
00:45:45,702 --> 00:45:46,953
I know how hard it is.

714
00:45:48,788 --> 00:45:51,416
If I can do something so people
won't go through the same thing,

715
00:45:52,750 --> 00:45:54,127
why not extend the help I can?

716
00:45:57,464 --> 00:45:58,798
There's no need for that.

717
00:46:01,217 --> 00:46:03,678
I won't be affected
by what Uncle Teddy has to say.

718
00:46:04,220 --> 00:46:07,849
Because I know that between us…

719
00:46:09,142 --> 00:46:11,728
I'm definitely kinder than he is.

720
00:46:21,154 --> 00:46:23,740
Ms. D, I already moved your 3 p.m. later.

721
00:46:24,324 --> 00:46:25,950
Just move everything to tomorrow.

722
00:46:26,034 --> 00:46:27,452
-Okay, will do.
-Okay.

723
00:46:33,958 --> 00:46:35,710
-Ms. D.
-Where is Patricia?

724
00:46:36,419 --> 00:46:38,630
The marketing department gave her a task.

725
00:46:39,214 --> 00:46:42,342
Uh, tell her to go to my office
right after, okay?

726
00:46:43,843 --> 00:46:45,178
I think…

727
00:46:47,472 --> 00:46:49,349
she's trying to avoid you, Ms. D.

728
00:46:50,850 --> 00:46:51,893
Because?

729
00:46:53,228 --> 00:46:54,521
With all due respect,

730
00:46:56,189 --> 00:47:00,235
we can't really blame Patricia
for feeling bad about what happened.

731
00:47:02,195 --> 00:47:04,280
It wasn't easy for her.

732
00:47:05,532 --> 00:47:07,617
She got humiliated in front of everyone.

733
00:47:09,577 --> 00:47:10,995
Is that what you think too?

734
00:47:11,871 --> 00:47:13,248
That I chose Teddy?

735
00:47:15,416 --> 00:47:17,669
It's an easy assumption to make, Ms. D.

736
00:47:18,419 --> 00:47:20,838
There's nothing easy
about the decisions I make, Enzo.

737
00:47:21,548 --> 00:47:23,925
There are lots of things to consider.

738
00:47:24,968 --> 00:47:27,095
I always need
to look at the bigger picture

739
00:47:27,178 --> 00:47:29,764
because there's so much at stake.

740
00:47:30,807 --> 00:47:33,017
It doesn't mean
I'm not doing anything about it.

741
00:47:34,852 --> 00:47:37,188
She knows you did that for the company

742
00:47:37,564 --> 00:47:38,773
and for the family.

743
00:47:38,856 --> 00:47:42,569
But Patricia is also your family, Ms. D.

744
00:47:43,319 --> 00:47:45,071
What are you trying to say, Enzo?

745
00:47:45,446 --> 00:47:46,990
I hope you don't get me wrong.

746
00:47:47,407 --> 00:47:49,909
I am not questioning your decisions.

747
00:47:50,368 --> 00:47:52,495
But Patricia doesn't see

748
00:47:52,579 --> 00:47:54,497
the bigger picture
you're talking about, Ms. D.

749
00:47:54,831 --> 00:47:59,168
She sees this whole situation
as your daughter.

750
00:48:01,045 --> 00:48:02,422
And she thinks…

751
00:48:04,215 --> 00:48:05,550
you made a choice

752
00:48:05,925 --> 00:48:07,051
and it wasn't her.

753
00:48:16,269 --> 00:48:17,478
-Oh!
-Oh! Sorry.

754
00:48:17,562 --> 00:48:19,564
-I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
-Sorry.

755
00:48:20,064 --> 00:48:21,274
Sorry.

756
00:48:23,860 --> 00:48:25,445
Good morning, ma'am. How can I help you?

757
00:48:26,279 --> 00:48:29,324
-I want to inquire about enrolling.
-Here.

758
00:48:46,466 --> 00:48:48,676
Why are you pacing back and forth?

759
00:48:49,135 --> 00:48:51,971
Mom and Sis aren't replying to me.

760
00:48:52,055 --> 00:48:54,307
Maybe Sis is just busy at work.

761
00:48:56,017 --> 00:48:57,018
Jena.

762
00:48:57,769 --> 00:48:58,853
What's this about

763
00:48:58,936 --> 00:49:01,606
that you need to bother
your mom and your sister?

764
00:49:02,565 --> 00:49:04,400
What do you want? Tell me.

765
00:49:04,484 --> 00:49:05,902
Uh, Dad…

766
00:49:07,528 --> 00:49:09,238
I need money.

767
00:49:09,656 --> 00:49:12,659
But it's for our school's fundraising.

768
00:49:12,742 --> 00:49:15,119
We organized a beauty pageant.

769
00:49:15,703 --> 00:49:16,954
How much do you need?

770
00:49:17,538 --> 00:49:19,415
-Three thousand pesos.
-What?

771
00:49:20,416 --> 00:49:22,293
Son of-- That's huge!

772
00:49:22,835 --> 00:49:24,629
Will that get you higher grades?

773
00:49:24,712 --> 00:49:26,089
Dad, please!

774
00:49:26,172 --> 00:49:29,759
Fine. Just don't bother them.

775
00:49:30,385 --> 00:49:33,680
If I win at gambling later,
I'll give you the money.

776
00:49:34,138 --> 00:49:36,724
Remember my classmate, Michelle?

777
00:49:36,808 --> 00:49:39,185
She said she'll pay for the venue.

778
00:49:39,602 --> 00:49:42,855
She'll rig the contest and win for sure.

779
00:49:43,481 --> 00:49:44,941
I hate it!

780
00:49:45,024 --> 00:49:47,193
Rich people always
get everything in their favor.

781
00:49:48,945 --> 00:49:50,279
Don't worry, dear,

782
00:49:51,072 --> 00:49:52,448
we'll recover from this.

783
00:49:53,074 --> 00:49:54,242
It's okay, Dad.

784
00:49:54,742 --> 00:49:56,744
I've accepted our situation.

785
00:49:57,620 --> 00:49:59,539
You don't believe me?

786
00:50:01,874 --> 00:50:03,584
Uh, I've got things to do.

787
00:50:12,385 --> 00:50:13,928
One… six.

788
00:50:14,011 --> 00:50:15,680
All right. Put it inside.

789
00:50:23,438 --> 00:50:24,981
Do you really think we're done?

790
00:50:27,024 --> 00:50:30,445
I know you're behind everything
that happened to me.

791
00:50:30,528 --> 00:50:34,157
All the lies they pointed at me
were your doing.

792
00:50:35,032 --> 00:50:37,535
You know, Teddy, I think you need a break.

793
00:50:37,618 --> 00:50:38,995
I know it's hot out.

794
00:50:39,746 --> 00:50:41,622
The heat may have gotten into your brain.

795
00:50:41,706 --> 00:50:42,749
No.

796
00:50:43,374 --> 00:50:44,792
I know that was you.

797
00:50:45,835 --> 00:50:47,295
The person who attacked my sister

798
00:50:48,045 --> 00:50:49,589
and the food poisoning
in the feeding program,

799
00:50:49,672 --> 00:50:50,715
that was all you.

800
00:50:51,382 --> 00:50:54,677
Careful now. You don't have any proof.

801
00:50:55,928 --> 00:50:57,138
That might cause you more harm.

802
00:50:59,223 --> 00:51:00,725
You really don't know me well.

803
00:51:02,310 --> 00:51:04,437
I don't know which ring of hell
you came from,

804
00:51:04,520 --> 00:51:06,397
but don't worry, I'll find out.

805
00:51:07,315 --> 00:51:08,733
You're the one who should be careful.

806
00:51:10,735 --> 00:51:12,487
Help Teddy.
He can't do all the heavy lifting.

807
00:51:22,288 --> 00:51:24,081
Have you found a side gig yet, bestie?

808
00:51:25,374 --> 00:51:27,293
I called the producer earlier.

809
00:51:27,376 --> 00:51:28,419
They said there's one.

810
00:51:28,503 --> 00:51:31,255
Oh? What role?
Maybe you can bring me along.

811
00:51:32,131 --> 00:51:33,424
Well, that's the thing, bestie.

812
00:51:33,508 --> 00:51:37,094
I tried asking the producer,
but they don't want to hire you anymore.

813
00:51:37,178 --> 00:51:39,055
It seems like you've been
blacklisted or something.

814
00:51:39,138 --> 00:51:42,183
And the director's been badmouthing you.

815
00:51:43,351 --> 00:51:44,811
Wait, I'm the victim here.

816
00:51:45,353 --> 00:51:47,021
I know, bestie.

817
00:51:47,438 --> 00:51:49,190
But you know how things work here.

818
00:51:49,273 --> 00:51:51,734
If they have it out for you
and you're not famous,

819
00:51:51,818 --> 00:51:52,860
there's nothing you can do.

820
00:51:52,944 --> 00:51:54,695
But why are you looking
for another gig anyway?

821
00:51:54,779 --> 00:51:56,531
I thought you were doing okay
with La Familia.

822
00:51:57,698 --> 00:51:59,659
I can't just rely on that.

823
00:52:02,703 --> 00:52:03,788
Besides…

824
00:52:04,831 --> 00:52:06,374
I want to go back to school.

825
00:52:07,542 --> 00:52:08,626
Well…

826
00:52:09,460 --> 00:52:11,671
Can you really juggle all of that?

827
00:52:12,255 --> 00:52:13,673
Oh, that's easy!

828
00:52:13,756 --> 00:52:15,341
It's not like you don't know me!

829
00:52:15,424 --> 00:52:17,260
I'm a hard worker, see!

830
00:52:18,553 --> 00:52:20,137
Oh, wow, you really are.

831
00:52:20,221 --> 00:52:21,222
A hard worker at eating buns.

832
00:52:21,305 --> 00:52:22,849
-I'm right, aren't I?
-Wow!

833
00:52:30,606 --> 00:52:32,275
Benjie, can't we leave yet?

834
00:52:32,650 --> 00:52:33,734
We have a flat tire, Ms. D.

835
00:52:34,193 --> 00:52:35,319
Again?

836
00:52:36,112 --> 00:52:38,447
There's a nail in the tire.

837
00:52:38,531 --> 00:52:40,032
-What?
-Right here.

838
00:52:44,912 --> 00:52:46,080
Diana.

839
00:52:46,831 --> 00:52:47,832
Did you get a flat tire?

840
00:52:48,457 --> 00:52:50,376
Do you think you can fix it?

841
00:52:50,459 --> 00:52:52,086
Yes, Ms. D. Uh…

842
00:52:52,169 --> 00:52:54,839
But I need to take the car
to a tire repair shop.

843
00:52:54,922 --> 00:52:56,257
It might take a while.

844
00:52:56,340 --> 00:52:58,801
You know what, I'll give you a ride.
You look tired, too.

845
00:52:59,302 --> 00:53:02,430
By the time Benjie finishes there,
you'll be tired and hungry.

846
00:53:02,513 --> 00:53:04,140
And there's traffic, too. Come on.

847
00:53:04,223 --> 00:53:05,850
Yes, Ms. D. After this,

848
00:53:05,933 --> 00:53:07,435
I'll bring the car straight home.

849
00:53:08,269 --> 00:53:09,604
-Okay.
-Let's go.

850
00:53:23,534 --> 00:53:26,454
You know, I have a reservation.

851
00:53:26,954 --> 00:53:28,414
Do you want to come with me?

852
00:53:28,497 --> 00:53:29,665
Or you know what, better yet,

853
00:53:29,749 --> 00:53:31,250
let's just go to your place.
It's quiet there.

854
00:53:32,376 --> 00:53:35,087
I've been missing home-cooked food.

855
00:53:35,171 --> 00:53:36,339
Excuse me.

856
00:53:37,590 --> 00:53:39,842
You're getting a little too casual
with me now.

857
00:53:41,260 --> 00:53:42,345
Is that a bad thing?

858
00:53:43,638 --> 00:53:45,139
Just don't get used to it.

859
00:53:45,222 --> 00:53:47,183
We're strictly co-workers.

860
00:53:48,184 --> 00:53:49,226
Yes, ma'am.

861
00:54:19,507 --> 00:54:23,344
Nanny, please prepare dinner for two.

862
00:54:28,683 --> 00:54:29,809
Good evening.

863
00:54:33,562 --> 00:54:34,772
Is it good?

864
00:54:34,855 --> 00:54:37,274
Sorry? Oh! The sushi?

865
00:54:37,858 --> 00:54:39,110
Yes, it's pretty good.

866
00:54:39,193 --> 00:54:40,403
That's good.

867
00:54:46,617 --> 00:54:47,660
Nanny?

868
00:54:48,411 --> 00:54:49,662
Nanny!

869
00:54:51,539 --> 00:54:53,124
Don't you have something to do?

870
00:54:56,252 --> 00:54:58,379
How about your duties?

871
00:55:00,756 --> 00:55:02,466
Oh, right. I do have something to do.

872
00:55:04,927 --> 00:55:07,471
-Call me whenever you need me.
-Yes! Yes.

873
00:55:11,142 --> 00:55:12,184
Are you close?

874
00:55:13,310 --> 00:55:14,687
Yes.

875
00:55:14,770 --> 00:55:17,273
She's been taking care of me
since I was a child.

876
00:55:17,356 --> 00:55:19,025
She's also been like a mother to me.

877
00:55:19,442 --> 00:55:20,985
So she's been with you
for a long time, huh?

878
00:55:21,068 --> 00:55:22,069
Mh-mm.

879
00:55:22,153 --> 00:55:23,863
Next time I come back here,

880
00:55:24,572 --> 00:55:26,115
I'll bring her a gift.

881
00:55:27,658 --> 00:55:28,784
Next time?

882
00:55:29,744 --> 00:55:31,037
She's such a great cook.

883
00:55:32,371 --> 00:55:33,998
I ate so much.

884
00:55:34,081 --> 00:55:36,709
Is it okay if I always eat here?

885
00:55:38,127 --> 00:55:41,464
Maybe when I come back,
there will be a sign posted there saying,

886
00:55:41,547 --> 00:55:44,258
"Ricardo Banned.
Reason: He eats too much."

887
00:55:44,675 --> 00:55:46,886
"Ricardo, you're such a PG."

888
00:55:48,679 --> 00:55:49,764
Do you know what PG means?

889
00:55:51,223 --> 00:55:52,600
Professional Glutton.

890
00:56:03,319 --> 00:56:05,654
Ricardo.

891
00:56:05,738 --> 00:56:07,239
It's getting late.

892
00:56:07,865 --> 00:56:09,283
Go home after you eat.

893
00:56:11,702 --> 00:56:12,745
Okay.

894
00:57:11,220 --> 00:57:13,264
Cala Soda is mine!

895
00:57:13,681 --> 00:57:15,141
I'm telling the truth!

896
00:57:15,224 --> 00:57:16,433
You're all thieves!

897
00:57:16,517 --> 00:57:20,354
All the evidence against Patricia
has been deleted.

898
00:57:20,437 --> 00:57:24,066
So everything can be pinned
on Cecilia Pineda.

899
00:57:24,400 --> 00:57:25,860
Make sure nothing about this gets out.

900
00:57:30,906 --> 00:57:33,075
I'm already gaining her trust.

901
00:57:34,869 --> 00:57:36,370
I'll avenge you.

902
00:57:41,917 --> 00:57:45,254
Ms. D wants you
to help her plan the new campaign.

903
00:57:45,337 --> 00:57:48,007
I'm just adding to her list
of disappointments.

904
00:57:48,090 --> 00:57:50,134
-Stop worrying!
-Do you have a thing with Enzo?

905
00:57:50,217 --> 00:57:52,761
-Where did that come from?
-Enzo and I used to be a thing.

906
00:57:52,845 --> 00:57:54,972
We've been separated for years.
Haven't you moved on?

907
00:57:55,055 --> 00:57:57,850
Do you really think
your relationship affects me?

908
00:57:58,684 --> 00:58:00,352
Someone sent me a message threatening me!

909
00:58:00,436 --> 00:58:03,063
-I'll protect you.
-Don't you think you trust him too much?

910
00:58:03,147 --> 00:58:05,399
I want to know who's doing this to me.

911
00:58:05,482 --> 00:58:07,318
Whoever did this is going to pay.

912
00:58:07,401 --> 00:58:08,611
I'll destroy them.
